## Decision memo (98-agent workflow, 30 claims x 3 refuters; 12 refuted and corrected)

# A5 audio and the SuperTuxKart hang: decision memo (#110 image, 2026-09-27)

Scope: Samsung A5 (`samsung,a5u-eur`), flashed image int-20260927. That image is the TEST-ONLY a5int STK layer on top of the #110 device image (claude/a5-integration f9b05d04), running kernel 7.3.0-0.rc2.28.msm8916 and Mesa 26.2.3-1.3.pocketfed. Nothing below was run on the phone. Tags: **[V]** means verified from source, RPMs, the image rpmdb or a host lab. **[I]** means inferred. **[U]** means unknown. "Lab" means an isolated x86_64 host replica running the same upstream PipeWire 1.6.9, WirePlumber 0.5.17, openal-soft 1.24.2-10 and feedbackd 0.8.9-4 (fc45 builds, the same NVRs as rawhide).

`$S` = `/tmp/claude-1000/-var-home-sam-src-pocketfed--claude-worktrees-exciting-cohen-dd1626/7945cb6c-8cd3-43c4-b856-4d4057d4caaa/scratchpad`

## TL;DR

- The working hypothesis ("no PipeWire sink at all") is **wrong**. feedbackd's `/usr/share/wireplumber/wireplumber.conf.d/media-role-nodes.conf` always creates six role-loopback `Audio/Sink` nodes. With no hardware sink behind them, WirePlumber 0.5.17 chain-links the loopbacks into the Alerts loopback, which has the `cork` action. STK's `Game` stream link to Multimedia is then corked, the stream never starts, and openal-soft 1.24.2 waits forever with no timeout. The lab reproduced the A5 stack exactly (lab s1/s10). On the A5 itself this is [I].
- There is no hardware sink because the only sound card on the A5 DT is QDSP6-on-modem. On #110 the modem is never started: blob-wrangler has no A5 config, so it fails, and `rmtfs` `Requires=` it. The modem firmware isn't present either. The kernel side (config, modules, packaging) is complete.
- Proposed fixes:
  - Immediate: ship a static low-priority null sink in `pipewire.conf.d` (lab-verified).
  - Defence in depth: patch openal-soft.
  - Real audio: blob-wrangler#19, an A5 UCM overlay and an S16LE rule.
  - Upstream: bugs in openal-soft (2), WirePlumber (2) and callaudiod.
- The callaudiod segfault is almost certainly the known NULL deref at cad-pulse.c:409. It is harmless for STK but has the same root cause (no card).

