## Refuted reader claims and what changed

| Reader claim | Correction (from refuters) | Effect on the picture |
|---|---|---|
| kernel-dt: card defers forever *because* `auto_boot=false` | `auto_boot` only blocks kernel autostart. rmtfs `-s` (or any root sysfs write) would start the modem. On #110 the start never happens (blob-wrangler fails, rmtfs dependency-fails), and it would fail anyway for lack of `mba.mbn`/`modem.mdt` | The fix is firmware plus blob-wrangler, not the kernel |
| kernel-dt: "the kernel requests mba.mbn and modem.mdt" (stated as happening) | On #110 nothing is ever requested; no request_firmware error is logged. Loading is sequential (MBA first, then `modem.mdt`). #19 copies blobs from the phone's partition at boot and does not ship them. `/var/lib/firmware-updates` is absent in the flashed image | Missing firmware is a second blocker behind blob-wrangler |
| image-userspace: openal pre-existed (cited `stk-trial-build2.log`) | Same substance; the correct log for the flashed image is `build-int-20260927.out:355-381` (the old log was the .26 trial) | Citation only |
| image-userspace: "nothing in the image guarantees a sink" | **Wrong.** feedbackd's `media-role-nodes.conf` guarantees six virtual loopback sinks, and they suppress auto_null | Overturns the "no sink" hypothesis; the hang is a WirePlumber policy trap, not a missing sink |
| pmos: "rmtfs -s is the only thing that starts it" | Any root write to the remoteproc `state` does it; rmtfs is only the only *shipped* starter | Minor |
| pmos: files "must be installed under conf.d/samsung-a2015/" | Only the entry point must be in conf.d, and it can be a symlink. HiFi.conf plus the `platforms/msm8916` and `codecs/msm8916-wcd` includes must sit at the ucm2 root (or the includes must be rewritten) | Shapes the overlay layout in §3(b)2 |
| pmos: no-modem mode dropped 2025-09-25 (MR 7075) | It stopped working 2024-10-26 when lk2nd went from 0.16.0 to 19.0 (MR 5691); MR 7075 only removed dead packages | No maintained firmware-free precedent anywhere |
| openal: "PipeWire won't start an unlinked stream" | The block is `NEED_CONFIGURE`, not the missing link. With `stream.dont-remix=true`, an unlinked stream runs on the Dummy-Driver and OpenAL returns | More precise mechanism, not a practical workaround |
| openal: the visible sink was "likely auto_null" | It was the Multimedia role loopback; auto_null is suppressed | Points the diagnosis at WirePlumber role linking |
| openal: the pulse backend would hang in `alcOpenDevice` | libpulse's 30 s reply timeout means a ~30 s stall, then NULL, then STK runs silently | `ALSOFT_DRIVERS=-pipewire,` is a usable (slow) workaround, if libpulse dlopens on rawhide ([U]) |
| wireplumber: without the loopbacks OpenAL "fails" | Without the loopbacks it opens auto_null and succeeds. The precondition that the A5 has no ALSA sink is still [I] | Pins the hang on feedbackd loopbacks combined with no hardware sink |
| callaudiod: crashes "whenever" a card-less, portless sink appears | Only for `device.class` absent or "sound" (:305-307), and only while no sink is adopted yet | Loopback sinks qualify (refuter repro), which gives the concrete A5 trigger |

